WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:11.929
We were in a store and a guy in that store...

2
00:00:12.012 --> 00:00:14.640
...told us to put our uniforms on.

3
00:00:14.681 --> 00:00:16.767
"What the hell are you talking about?"

4
00:00:17.976 --> 00:00:22.272
He says. "The USA is in a war with Japan."

5
00:00:22.773 --> 00:00:24.149
We couldn't believe it.

6
00:00:24.233 --> 00:00:26.276
Well. our country was attacked.

7
00:00:26.652 --> 00:00:27.611
It's different.

8
00:00:27.653 --> 00:00:29.530
It wasn't like Korea or Vietnam.

9
00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:31.114
We were attacked.

10
00:00:32.032 --> 00:00:34.826
And. you know. it was a feeling that...

11
00:00:35.410 --> 00:00:38.330
...maybe. we're just dumb country people
but...

12
00:00:38.455 --> 00:00:41.583
...where I come from a lot of us volunteered.

13
00:00:41.667 --> 00:00:43.961
"Who would like to volunteer for the Tank
Corps?

14
00:00:43.961 --> 00:00:46.588
"Who would like to volunteer for the Air
Force?

15
00:00:46.588 --> 00:00:49.841
"Who would like to volunteer for the Navy?" or
whatever.

16
00:00:49.967 --> 00:00:51.343
And then. they said:

17
00:00:51.426 --> 00:00:53.804
"Who would like to volunteer for the
Airborne?"

18
00:00:54.221 --> 00:00:56.473
Somebody says. "What the hell's the Airborne?"

19
00:00:56.557 --> 00:00:57.724
Nobody ever heard of it.

20
00:00:57.849 --> 00:01:00.102
We came from a small. small town.

21
00:01:00.310 --> 00:01:04.398
And three fellows in that town that were 4F...

22
00:01:04.439 --> 00:01:07.276
...committed suicide because they couldn't go.

23
00:01:08.318 --> 00:01:09.653
A different time.

24
00:01:09.695 --> 00:01:10.821
I did things.

25
00:01:10.946 --> 00:01:12.781
I didn't do them for medals.

26
00:01:12.823 --> 00:01:17.661
I didn't do them for accolades. I did 'em
because it's what had to be done.

27
00:01:17.828 --> 00:01:19.705
The guy says. "would you jump out of
airplanes?

28
00:01:19.830 --> 00:01:21.456
"You know. you got all your army equipment...

29
00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:24.334
"...and you jump out of airplanes. to fight
the enemy."

30
00:01:24.710 --> 00:01:26.670
These guys. they said. "Go to hell."

31
00:01:26.712 --> 00:01:28.338
Nobody put up their hands.

32
00:01:28.422 --> 00:01:30.340
And then. I don't know what it was brought it
up...

33
00:01:30.465 --> 00:01:33.343
...but the guy giving the speech was saying:

34
00:01:33.427 --> 00:01:36.054
"But you get paid $50 a month more."

35
00:01:36.096 --> 00:01:38.181
So. that made it a hundred bucks.

36
00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:46.074
Do you want subtitles for any video?
-=[ ai.OpenSubtitles.com ]=-

37
00:04:36.902 --> 00:04:38.987
I want a whiff of chicken pie.

38
00:04:39.154 --> 00:04:41.239
Okay. boys. let's get this gear stowed.

39
00:05:01.635 --> 00:05:05.180
Fox Company...we go in five.

40
00:05:13.313 --> 00:05:16.274
"In the name of the Father..."

41
00:05:22.322 --> 00:05:24.324
1st Platoon. draw small arms.

42
00:05:25.325 --> 00:05:27.160
Do you need a hand. Lieutenant?

43
00:05:28.286 --> 00:05:31.706
Easy Company! Listen up!

44
00:05:31.790 --> 00:05:33.583
Gather up around me.

45
00:05:33.834 --> 00:05:36.086
Just move it up. Come on. gentlemen.

46
00:05:36.419 --> 00:05:37.671
Let's go!

47
00:05:41.424 --> 00:05:44.845
Now. the Channel coast is socked in with rain
and fog.

48
00:05:44.970 --> 00:05:46.555
High winds on the drop zone.

49
00:05:46.972 --> 00:05:49.099
No jump tonight.

50
00:05:49.724 --> 00:05:51.726
The invasion has been postponed.

51
00:05:51.810 --> 00:05:54.938
We're on a 24-hour stand-down. Son of a bitch.

52
00:05:54.980 --> 00:05:56.731
Drill sergeants. take charge.

53
00:05:58.733 --> 00:06:02.070
Well. this is quite a surprise.

54
00:06:02.320 --> 00:06:03.446
Not particularly.

55
00:06:03.572 --> 00:06:05.824
It so happens I rather expected it.

56
00:06:06.324 --> 00:06:12.205
Well. I can't see how you people can pass up
$80.000 for the Cause

57
00:06:12.247 --> 00:06:13.748
For whose cause?

58
00:06:14.207 --> 00:06:16.376
If you're so interested in serving a cause...

59
00:06:16.459 --> 00:06:18.211
...why don't you join the Army?

60
00:06:41.276 --> 00:06:43.236
I think it's clearing up.

61
00:06:46.489 --> 00:06:47.782
You think it's clearing up?

62
00:06:49.242 --> 00:06:50.368
No.

63
00:06:51.786 --> 00:06:53.538
I think it's clearing up.

64
00:06:56.166 --> 00:06:57.292
How are your men?

65
00:06:58.418 --> 00:06:59.920
They'll be fine.

66
00:07:05.800 --> 00:07:07.427
5:00 in New York.

67
00:07:08.178 --> 00:07:09.638
4:00 in Chicago.

68
00:07:11.306 --> 00:07:13.683
Happy hour. huh?
Yeah.

69
00:07:14.142 --> 00:07:15.310
Happy hour.

70
00:07:15.810 --> 00:07:17.145
A couple of drinks.

71
00:07:17.520 --> 00:07:19.773
Maybe an early dinner before the theater.

72
00:07:26.696 --> 00:07:29.199
A civilized place for civilized men.

73
00:07:34.287 --> 00:07:36.831
Should've been born earlier. Nix.

74
00:07:37.457 --> 00:07:39.542
What. and give up all this?

75
00:07:54.057 --> 00:07:56.476
We'll go to Chicago. I'll take you there.

76
00:07:57.227 --> 00:07:58.478
Yeah.

77
00:07:59.854 --> 00:08:01.606
We'll see.

78
00:08:10.115 --> 00:08:12.200
Actually. you know who's from there?

79
00:08:12.242 --> 00:08:14.619
Who? Oh. him.

80
00:08:15.745 --> 00:08:19.249
712 days of that son of a bitch and here we
are.

81
00:08:45.775 --> 00:08:49.571
You people are at the position of attention.

82
00:08:57.328 --> 00:09:01.791
Private Perconte. have you been blousing your
trousers over your boots like a paratrooper?

83
00:09:01.833 --> 00:09:02.667
No. sir.

84
00:09:02.709 --> 00:09:04.919
Then explain the creases at the bottom.

85
00:09:05.295 --> 00:09:06.337
No excuse. sir.

86
00:09:06.421 --> 00:09:09.215
Volunteering for the Parachute Infantry is one
thing...

87
00:09:09.299 --> 00:09:11.801
...but you've got a long way to prove you
belong here.

88
00:09:11.843 --> 00:09:13.970
Your weekend pass is revoked.

89
00:09:14.679 --> 00:09:16.723
Name? Luz. George.

90
00:09:18.224 --> 00:09:19.809
Dirt in the rear side aperture.

91
00:09:19.851 --> 00:09:21.227
Pass revoked.

92
00:09:33.823 --> 00:09:36.367
When did you sew on these chevrons. Sergeant
Lipton?

93
00:09:36.451 --> 00:09:38.203
Yesterday. sir.

94
00:09:38.244 --> 00:09:40.371
Long enough to notice this. Revoked.

95
00:09:40.830 --> 00:09:41.706
Sir.

96
00:09:43.750 --> 00:09:44.501
Name?

97
00:09:44.584 --> 00:09:45.960
Malarkey. Donald G.

98
00:09:46.753 --> 00:09:48.630
Malarkey's slang for bullshit. isn't it?

99
00:09:48.755 --> 00:09:49.631
Yes. sir.

100
00:09:51.591 --> 00:09:54.344
Rust on the butt plate hinge spring. Private
Bullshit.

101
00:09:54.511 --> 00:09:55.762
Revoked.

102
00:09:57.222 --> 00:09:58.014
Name?

103
00:09:58.098 --> 00:09:59.516
Liebgott. Joseph D.. sir.

104
00:10:02.644 --> 00:10:04.354
Rusty bayonet. Liebgott.

105
00:10:05.522 --> 00:10:06.606
You want to kill Germans?

106
00:10:06.648 --> 00:10:07.398
Yes. sir.

107
00:10:07.524 --> 00:10:08.775
Not with this.

108
00:10:10.777 --> 00:10:14.405
I wouldn't take this rusty piece of shit to
war.

109
00:10:14.531 --> 00:10:17.784
And I will not take you to war in your
condition.

110
00:10:17.867 --> 00:10:20.286
Now. thanks to these men and their
infractions...

111
00:10:20.370 --> 00:10:23.123
...every man in the company who had a weekend
pass...

112
00:10:23.414 --> 00:10:24.791
...has lost it.

113
00:10:27.544 --> 00:10:30.672
Change into your PT gear. we're running
Currahee.

114
00:10:33.675 --> 00:10:34.801
2nd Platoon. fall out.

115
00:10:34.926 --> 00:10:35.927
We have two minutes.

116
00:10:36.010 --> 00:10:37.053
Fall out!

117
00:10:42.392 --> 00:10:44.185
I ain't going up that hill.

118
00:10:45.520 --> 00:10:49.190
Perconte. what are you thinking of blousing
your pants?

119
00:10:49.190 --> 00:10:50.316
Shut up. okay?

120
00:10:50.400 --> 00:10:51.442
He gigged everyone.

121
00:10:51.568 --> 00:10:52.819
You should know better.

122
00:10:52.819 --> 00:10:54.320
Don't give him no excuses.

123
00:10:54.320 --> 00:10:55.572
Excuses?

124
00:10:55.655 --> 00:10:57.782
Why don't you come here. look at these
trousers...

125
00:10:57.824 --> 00:10:59.701
...get down and tell me if there's a crease?

126
00:10:59.701 --> 00:11:01.452
Let's go on the road in PT formation.

127
00:11:01.578 --> 00:11:03.037
Let's move. move. move!

128
00:11:04.080 --> 00:11:06.916
Perconte. let's go. Perconte.

129
00:11:10.295 --> 00:11:13.464
Private White. why are you not in your PT
gear?

130
00:11:17.844 --> 00:11:19.846
I asked you a question. Private.

131
00:11:37.071 --> 00:11:39.073
Oh. Easy Company.

132
00:11:39.115 --> 00:11:40.491
While you're running. don't worry.

133
00:11:40.575 --> 00:11:42.368
We'll take your dames to the movies.

134
00:11:42.368 --> 00:11:44.996
Yeah. good. they need some female company.

135
00:11:51.252 --> 00:11:52.462
Where do we run?

136
00:11:52.503 --> 00:11:53.713
Currahee.

137
00:11:53.838 --> 00:11:54.881
What does "Currahee" mean?

138
00:11:55.006 --> 00:11:56.132
We stand alone.

139
00:11:56.257 --> 00:11:57.759
How far up. how far down?

140
00:11:57.842 --> 00:11:59.636
Three miles up. three miles down.

141
00:11:59.886 --> 00:12:01.387
And what company is this?

142
00:12:01.512 --> 00:12:02.889
Easy Company.

143
00:12:02.972 --> 00:12:05.350
And what do we do? Stand alone.

144
00:12:05.391 --> 00:12:08.394
Do not help that man! Do not help that man!

145
00:12:08.770 --> 00:12:10.480
We do not stop.

146
00:12:11.981 --> 00:12:14.901
You've got 30 minutes to get to the top of
this mountain...

147
00:12:15.360 --> 00:12:17.862
...if you want to serve in the Paratroopers.

148
00:12:18.279 --> 00:12:20.907
Hi-ho. Silver!

149
00:12:46.808 --> 00:12:47.934
You can make it up there.

150
00:12:48.059 --> 00:12:48.810
Come on.

151
00:12:48.810 --> 00:12:49.936
Come on. Alley. let's go.

152
00:12:50.061 --> 00:12:51.187
Come on. Guarnere.

153
00:12:51.271 --> 00:12:52.522
Christenson. come on.

154
00:12:52.563 --> 00:12:55.066
I never thought I'd see the day. Private Wynn.

155
00:12:55.942 --> 00:12:59.070
We are coming on 23 minutes.

156
00:12:59.195 --> 00:13:02.699
That may be good enough for the rest of the
506...

157
00:13:02.782 --> 00:13:05.576
...but that is not good enough for Easy
Company.

158
00:13:15.962 --> 00:13:18.339
We can make it. we can do this. come on.

159
00:13:47.493 --> 00:13:49.370
I'm going to say something.

160
00:13:49.746 --> 00:13:50.872
To who?

161
00:13:54.459 --> 00:13:55.752
Lieutenant Winters.

162
00:13:56.586 --> 00:13:58.212
What is it?

163
00:13:58.254 --> 00:14:00.131
Permission to speak. sir?

164
00:14:00.256 --> 00:14:01.466
Permission granted.

165
00:14:01.507 --> 00:14:03.593
Sir. we got nine companies. sir.

166
00:14:04.135 --> 00:14:05.386
That we do.

167
00:14:06.512 --> 00:14:08.139
How come we're the only company...

168
00:14:08.264 --> 00:14:12.643
...marching every Friday night. 12 miles. full
pack in the pitch dark?

169
00:14:12.727 --> 00:14:14.771
Why do you think. Private Randleman?

170
00:14:15.646 --> 00:14:17.732
Lieutenant Sobel hates us. sir.

171
00:14:22.362 --> 00:14:25.656
Lieutenant Sobel does not hate
Easy Company. Private Randleman.

172
00:14:27.033 --> 00:14:28.785
He just hates you.

173
00:14:29.369 --> 00:14:31.037
Thank you. sir.

174
00:14:33.539 --> 00:14:35.041
He hates him back.

175
00:14:35.792 --> 00:14:37.377
He hates you. too. Muck.

176
00:14:37.418 --> 00:14:41.047
Lieutenant Winters. I want canteens out of
belts with the caps unscrewed.

177
00:14:41.172 --> 00:14:43.132
Easy Company. canteens out and open.

178
00:14:43.299 --> 00:14:46.386
On my command. they will pour the contents
onto the ground.

179
00:14:46.427 --> 00:14:49.013
On the CO's order. you will upend your
canteen.

180
00:14:49.055 --> 00:14:50.181
Now. Lieutenant.

181
00:14:50.264 --> 00:14:51.307
Pour them.

182
00:14:57.563 --> 00:14:58.648
Who is this?

183
00:14:59.774 --> 00:15:00.942
Christenson.

184
00:15:01.067 --> 00:15:03.319
Why is there no water in your canteen?

185
00:15:03.444 --> 00:15:05.154
You drank from your canteen. didn't you?

186
00:15:05.446 --> 00:15:07.073
Lieutenant.
Yes. sir.

187
00:15:07.156 --> 00:15:11.953
Was this man ordered to not drink from his
canteen during the Friday night march?

188
00:15:12.078 --> 00:15:12.912
He was. sir.

189
00:15:12.954 --> 00:15:15.456
Private Christenson. you have disobeyed a
direct order.

190
00:15:15.581 --> 00:15:16.707
You will fill your canteen...

191
00:15:16.833 --> 00:15:20.336
...and repeat all 12 miles of the march
immediately.

192
00:15:20.420 --> 00:15:21.337
Yes. sir.

193
00:15:21.421 --> 00:15:22.588
Fall out!

194
00:15:31.305 --> 00:15:34.100
What in the name of God are you doing with my
company?

195
00:15:34.684 --> 00:15:38.563
You're late and you allow troopers to disobey
direct orders?

196
00:15:38.604 --> 00:15:39.981
No excuse. sir.

197
00:15:41.232 --> 00:15:43.818
You're making me look bad. Lieutenant.

198
00:15:43.860 --> 00:15:47.613
This is not Dog Company. This is not Fox
Company.

199
00:15:47.613 --> 00:15:50.241
This is Easy Company.

200
00:15:50.700 --> 00:15:52.618
Under my command. this will be the first...

201
00:15:52.618 --> 00:15:54.871
...and finest company in this regiment.

202
00:15:56.956 --> 00:15:58.958
I want the names of six men.

203
00:15:59.959 --> 00:16:04.755
Their infractions and your disciplinary
recommendations on my desk by 0130.

204
00:16:04.839 --> 00:16:06.090
Is that clear?

205
00:16:07.341 --> 00:16:09.093
What infractions. sir?

206
00:16:10.136 --> 00:16:11.888
Find some.

207
00:16:16.142 --> 00:16:17.768
So. what'd you do?

208
00:16:18.269 --> 00:16:20.771
Picked six men and gave them latrine duty.

209
00:16:21.147 --> 00:16:22.398
The lucky six?

210
00:16:22.482 --> 00:16:25.401
McDowell. Toye. Perconte.

211
00:16:25.526 --> 00:16:28.738
Lipton. Muck and Guarnere.

212
00:16:29.030 --> 00:16:30.239
Why them?

213
00:16:30.281 --> 00:16:31.657
It was their turn.

214
00:16:32.783 --> 00:16:34.494
Sobel's a genius.

215
00:16:34.535 --> 00:16:36.787
I had a headmaster just like him in prep
school.

216
00:16:36.871 --> 00:16:38.122
I know the type.

217
00:16:38.372 --> 00:16:39.540
Lewis.

218
00:16:39.665 --> 00:16:42.293
Michelangelo's a genius. Beethoven's a genius.

219
00:16:42.376 --> 00:16:46.130
You know a man in this company who wouldn't
double-time Currahee with a full pack...

220
00:16:46.172 --> 00:16:48.674
...just to piss in that guy's morning coffee?

221
00:16:49.884 --> 00:16:51.552
Let's go. let's go.

222
00:16:54.180 --> 00:16:55.515
Stand in the door.

223
00:16:56.057 --> 00:16:57.767
1.000
. 2.000.

224
00:16:57.808 --> 00:17:00.436
You just broke both your legs. Private Gordon.

225
00:17:00.686 --> 00:17:02.146
Are you trying to get killed?

226
00:17:02.313 --> 00:17:03.564
No. sir.

227
00:17:04.690 --> 00:17:06.108
Stand in the door.

228
00:17:20.414 --> 00:17:21.415
Shit.

229
00:17:27.922 --> 00:17:28.798
To the wall.

230
00:17:28.881 --> 00:17:29.757
Over as a team.

231
00:17:29.799 --> 00:17:31.676
Go on. against the wall.

232
00:17:32.885 --> 00:17:35.054
Jesus. what the hell is this?

233
00:17:35.137 --> 00:17:37.139
That's pig guts. boy.

234
00:17:41.185 --> 00:17:42.812
Goddamn it!

235
00:17:44.564 --> 00:17:46.023
Why are you here. Private Gordon?

236
00:17:46.065 --> 00:17:47.191
To be in the Airborne. sir.

237
00:17:47.191 --> 00:17:49.694
I don't believe you. Why are you here. Private
Gordon?

238
00:17:49.819 --> 00:17:51.195
To be in the Airborne. sir.

239
00:17:51.279 --> 00:17:55.074
You have 50 minutes to the top and back. and I
will be watching you.

240
00:17:56.200 --> 00:17:57.702
What are you waiting for?

241
00:18:39.327 --> 00:18:43.748
Easy Company has the finest performance record
in the entire 2nd Battalion.

242
00:18:44.248 --> 00:18:47.376
I believe every bit of that is thanks to you.

243
00:18:48.336 --> 00:18:49.712
Congratulations. Captain Sobel.

244
00:18:49.754 --> 00:18:51.005
Thank you. sir.

245
00:18:52.381 --> 00:18:55.760
Isn't that Lieutenant Winters leading Easy
Company in PT?

246
00:18:56.761 --> 00:18:58.262
Yes. sir.

247
00:18:58.471 --> 00:18:59.972
He's a damned good man.

248
00:19:00.014 --> 00:19:02.391
I was planning on giving him a set of these
today.

249
00:19:02.475 --> 00:19:06.145
Why don't you do it? He'd be proud to get them
from you.

250
00:19:11.776 --> 00:19:13.778
Pornography. contraband.

251
00:19:17.531 --> 00:19:20.660
Non-regulation clothing. contraband.

252
00:19:21.869 --> 00:19:26.165
This man had 200 prophylactic kits in his
footlocker.

253
00:19:26.415 --> 00:19:30.795
How in the name of God was he going to have
the strength to fight the war?

254
00:19:31.504 --> 00:19:33.798
How is it Private Tipper...

255
00:19:34.173 --> 00:19:37.635
...has spare time for so much correspondence?

256
00:19:38.678 --> 00:19:41.931
Captain. are personal letters to be considered
contraband?

257
00:19:43.557 --> 00:19:46.185
These men aren't paratroopers yet. Lieutenant.

258
00:19:46.310 --> 00:19:48.437
They have no personal property.

259
00:19:52.566 --> 00:19:53.818
What is this?

260
00:19:55.319 --> 00:19:56.570
Anybody?

261
00:19:57.697 --> 00:19:59.198
It's a can of peaches. sir.

262
00:19:59.407 --> 00:20:03.661
Lieutenant Nixon thinks this is a can of
peaches.

263
00:20:03.703 --> 00:20:05.079
That is incorrect. Lieutenant.

264
00:20:05.204 --> 00:20:07.039
Your weekend pass is cancelled.

265
00:20:07.081 --> 00:20:11.335
This is United States Army property...

266
00:20:11.711 --> 00:20:16.215
...which was taken. without authorization.
from my mess facility...

267
00:20:16.340 --> 00:20:19.844
...and I will not tolerate thievery in my
unit.

268
00:20:19.927 --> 00:20:21.470
Whose footlocker is this?

269
00:20:21.554 --> 00:20:23.097
Private Parks. sir.

270
00:20:24.098 --> 00:20:25.558
Get rid of him.

271
00:20:27.226 --> 00:20:28.978
All weekend passes are cancelled.

272
00:20:29.061 --> 00:20:30.855
Officers included.

273
00:20:33.107 --> 00:20:34.567
Carry on.

274
00:20:38.821 --> 00:20:40.448
Lieutenant Winters.

275
00:20:48.581 --> 00:20:51.250
Colonel Sink has seen fit to promote you.

276
00:20:52.126 --> 00:20:55.463
As First Lieutenant. you'll serve as my
executive officer.

277
00:20:56.505 --> 00:20:57.840
Congratulations.

278
00:20:58.257 --> 00:20:59.341
Thank you. sir.

279
00:20:59.383 --> 00:21:06.390
And. as a test of your organizational skills
and command potential...

280
00:21:06.474 --> 00:21:10.644
...I am designating you mess officer for 14
days.

281
00:21:11.729 --> 00:21:14.607
Report to the mess kitchen at 0515 hours.

282
00:21:14.648 --> 00:21:17.485
Company breakfast to be served at 0600.

283
00:21:18.652 --> 00:21:20.154
Yes. sir.

284
00:21:21.405 --> 00:21:25.034
And. Dick. there's rain forecast tomorrow...

285
00:21:25.242 --> 00:21:30.122
...so the company will have a light afternoon
of lecture and classroom instruction.

286
00:21:32.666 --> 00:21:36.170
I think a special meal before their afternoon
off...

287
00:21:36.295 --> 00:21:37.922
...would be a welcome change of pace.

288
00:21:37.922 --> 00:21:39.173
Would you agree?

289
00:21:39.256 --> 00:21:40.132
Yes. sir.

290
00:21:41.675 --> 00:21:42.927
I like spaghetti.

291
00:21:52.895 --> 00:21:54.522
Hold on. more coming.

292
00:21:55.147 --> 00:21:56.816
These guys are packing it away.

293
00:22:08.327 --> 00:22:09.537
This stuff is orange.

294
00:22:09.954 --> 00:22:12.081
Spaghetti ain't supposed to be orange.

295
00:22:12.164 --> 00:22:13.332
This ain't spaghetti.

296
00:22:13.457 --> 00:22:15.459
This is army noodles with ketchup.

297
00:22:15.709 --> 00:22:17.461
You ain't got to eat it.

298
00:22:17.545 --> 00:22:19.839
Oh. come on. Gonorrhea. as a fellow Italian...

299
00:22:19.922 --> 00:22:22.466
...you know that calling this spaghetti is a
mortal sin.

300
00:22:22.591 --> 00:22:24.468
I'll have it. No. I'm eating here.

301
00:22:24.468 --> 00:22:25.845
Hey. get out of here.

302
00:22:27.680 --> 00:22:29.807
Orders changed. get up!

303
00:22:29.932 --> 00:22:31.475
Lectures are cancelled.

304
00:22:31.559 --> 00:22:33.853
Easy Company is running up Currahee.

305
00:22:33.936 --> 00:22:35.479
Move. move!

306
00:22:38.732 --> 00:22:41.235
Three miles up. three miles down.

307
00:22:41.735 --> 00:22:44.196
Hi-ho. Silver!

308
00:22:44.989 --> 00:22:46.699
Let's go. let's go.

309
00:22:51.370 --> 00:22:53.998
You're a washout. Private Hoobler!

310
00:22:53.998 --> 00:22:56.375
You should pack up both your ears and go home.

311
00:22:56.500 --> 00:22:58.002
Looks like Gordon's done.

312
00:22:58.127 --> 00:22:59.879
Aren't you. Gordon. You finished?

313
00:22:59.879 --> 00:23:02.006
You do not deserve to get your wings.

314
00:23:02.089 --> 00:23:04.008
Private Randleman. you look tired.

315
00:23:04.633 --> 00:23:07.845
There's an ambulance waiting for you at the
bottom of the hill.

316
00:23:07.887 --> 00:23:10.139
It can all be over right now.

317
00:23:10.222 --> 00:23:12.600
No more pain. no more Currahee.

318
00:23:13.225 --> 00:23:15.019
No more Captain Sobel.

319
00:23:15.227 --> 00:23:18.856
"We pull upon the risers We fall upon the
grass

320
00:23:18.898 --> 00:23:21.984
"We never land upon our feet We always hit our
ass

321
00:23:22.151 --> 00:23:25.529
"Hide tidee. Christ almighty Who the hell are
we?

322
00:23:25.613 --> 00:23:29.033
"Zim zam. goddamn! We're Airborne Infantry

323
00:23:29.158 --> 00:23:32.286
"We pull upon the risers We fall upon the
grass

324
00:23:32.411 --> 00:23:35.372
"We never land upon our feet We always hit our
ass

325
00:23:35.748 --> 00:23:38.876
"Hide tidee. Christ almighty Who the hell are
we?

326
00:23:39.043 --> 00:23:42.296
"Zim zam. goddamn! We're Airborne Infantry"

327
00:23:56.310 --> 00:23:59.021
So. do we feel like we're ready to be army
paratroopers?

328
00:23:59.063 --> 00:24:00.272
Yes. Sergeant.

329
00:24:00.439 --> 00:24:01.690
I hope so.

330
00:24:02.066 --> 00:24:06.445
This'll be the first of five exits from a C-47
aircraft scheduled for today.

331
00:24:06.946 --> 00:24:08.197
Get ready!

332
00:24:09.573 --> 00:24:11.075
Stand up!

333
00:24:11.659 --> 00:24:12.576
Hook up!

334
00:24:12.660 --> 00:24:15.579
Upon successful completion of your fifth and
final jump...

335
00:24:15.704 --> 00:24:18.040
...you'll be certified army paratroopers.

336
00:24:18.165 --> 00:24:20.084
Check equipment!

337
00:24:21.585 --> 00:24:23.921
Sound off for equipment check!

338
00:24:24.546 --> 00:24:25.714
Nine okay.

339
00:24:25.923 --> 00:24:26.924
Eight okay.

340
00:24:26.966 --> 00:24:28.092
Seven okay.

341
00:24:28.717 --> 00:24:30.302
Six okay.

342
00:24:30.803 --> 00:24:32.179
Five okay.

343
00:24:32.471 --> 00:24:33.722
Four okay.

344
00:24:33.806 --> 00:24:35.099
Three okay.

345
00:24:35.099 --> 00:24:35.975
Two okay.

346
00:24:36.100 --> 00:24:37.059
One okay.

347
00:24:37.101 --> 00:24:39.853
There'll be a lot of men dropping from the sky
today.

348
00:24:40.104 --> 00:24:42.856
Hopefully. under deployed canopies.

349
00:24:42.940 --> 00:24:44.608
Stand in the door!

350
00:24:47.486 --> 00:24:50.114
I guarantee you're going to love it.
Lieutenant.

351
00:24:50.698 --> 00:24:51.991
Go. go!

352
00:24:52.116 --> 00:24:54.076
Jumping from 1.000 feet AGL...

353
00:24:54.493 --> 00:24:57.496
...in sticks of 12 jumpers per aircraft.

354
00:24:57.871 --> 00:25:01.083
All you have to do is remember what you were
taught...

355
00:25:01.458 --> 00:25:04.336
...and I guarantee you. gravity will take care
of the rest.

356
00:25:04.378 --> 00:25:07.464
Go. go. go. go!

357
00:25:11.635 --> 00:25:14.096
Go. go. go!

358
00:25:18.350 --> 00:25:21.145
Go. go. go!

359
00:25:48.922 --> 00:25:50.299
Damn it.

360
00:25:51.508 --> 00:25:53.761
And. gentlemen. rest assured...

361
00:25:53.802 --> 00:25:57.431
...any refusals in the aircraft or at the
door...

362
00:25:58.557 --> 00:26:02.686
...and I guarantee you. you will be out of the
Airborne.

363
00:26:02.936 --> 00:26:04.188
Four okay.

364
00:26:04.438 --> 00:26:05.314
Three okay.

365
00:26:05.397 --> 00:26:06.023
Two okay.

366
00:26:06.065 --> 00:26:06.899
One okay.

367
00:26:07.399 --> 00:26:08.692
Stand in the door.

368
00:26:11.320 --> 00:26:12.571
Go!

369
00:26:24.083 --> 00:26:28.545
1.000. 2.000. 3.000.
4.000. 5.000. 6.000 ...

370
00:26:28.587 --> 00:26:31.173
...7.000. 8.000. 9.000!

371
00:26:35.219 --> 00:26:36.845
Hi-ho. Silver!

372
00:26:42.935 --> 00:26:45.729
Now just think. if you had any class or style
like me...

373
00:26:45.729 --> 00:26:47.856
...somebody might mistake you for somebody.

374
00:26:47.940 --> 00:26:49.858
You mean like your fucking sergeant?

375
00:26:51.610 --> 00:26:53.112
I'm just kidding.

376
00:26:56.073 --> 00:26:57.366
Congratulations. Martin.

377
00:26:57.449 --> 00:27:01.453
Corporal Toye. there will be no leaning in my
company.

378
00:27:02.621 --> 00:27:05.249
Are those dusty jump wings?

379
00:27:05.749 --> 00:27:09.211
How do you expect to slay the Huns with dust
on your jump wings?

380
00:27:09.628 --> 00:27:11.880
Luz. just give me a drink.

381
00:27:13.966 --> 00:27:15.759
Hell of an idea. Joe.

382
00:27:15.884 --> 00:27:17.386
There you go.

383
00:27:18.720 --> 00:27:21.140
Three miles up. three miles down.

384
00:27:22.975 --> 00:27:24.393
Ten-hut!

385
00:27:33.902 --> 00:27:35.654
Well. at ease. paratroopers.

386
00:27:37.406 --> 00:27:39.032
Good evening. Easy Company.

387
00:27:39.116 --> 00:27:40.742
Evening. sir.

388
00:27:40.993 --> 00:27:43.412
Now. Parachute Infantry is a brand-new
concept...

389
00:27:43.537 --> 00:27:45.164
...in American military history.

390
00:27:45.289 --> 00:27:48.167
But. by God. the 506 is going to forge that
brand-new concept...

391
00:27:48.292 --> 00:27:49.251
...into victory.

392
00:27:49.293 --> 00:27:50.419
Yes. sir.

393
00:27:50.544 --> 00:27:54.256
I want you to know that I'm damned proud of
each and every one of you.

394
00:27:54.298 --> 00:27:56.550
Now. you deserve this party.

395
00:27:57.176 --> 00:27:58.260
Thank you. Sergeant Grant.

396
00:27:58.302 --> 00:27:59.428
Sir.

397
00:27:59.511 --> 00:28:03.182
So. I want you to have fun and remember our
motto:

398
00:28:03.307 --> 00:28:04.391
Currahee!

399
00:28:04.433 --> 00:28:06.185
Currahee!

400
00:28:32.836 --> 00:28:34.087
Petty.

401
00:28:34.463 --> 00:28:35.339
Map.

402
00:28:35.422 --> 00:28:36.340
Come on.

403
00:28:36.673 --> 00:28:38.050
Ah. Christ.

404
00:28:51.230 --> 00:28:52.981
We're in the wrong position.

405
00:28:56.318 --> 00:28:57.736
We're in the wrong position.

406
00:28:57.819 --> 00:28:59.988
We're textbook position for ambush. sir.

407
00:29:00.113 --> 00:29:03.492
We should sit tight. let the enemy team come
into our killing zone.

408
00:29:03.575 --> 00:29:04.993
They're right out there somewhere.

409
00:29:05.452 --> 00:29:06.495
Let's just get them.

410
00:29:06.578 --> 00:29:08.372
Sir. we have perfect cover here.

411
00:29:08.580 --> 00:29:10.499
Lieutenant. deploy your troops.

412
00:29:13.252 --> 00:29:16.004
2nd Platoon. move out.

413
00:29:16.255 --> 00:29:17.089
What?

414
00:29:17.130 --> 00:29:18.257
Tactical column.

415
00:29:38.026 --> 00:29:42.030
Captain. you've just been killed. along with
95 percent of your company.

416
00:29:42.364 --> 00:29:43.740
Your outfit?

417
00:29:44.783 --> 00:29:47.411
Easy Company. 2nd Battalion. 506th.

418
00:29:51.123 --> 00:29:55.544
Leave three wounded men on the ground and
report back to the assembly area.

419
00:29:56.295 --> 00:29:58.046
Goddamn it.

420
00:30:03.051 --> 00:30:04.928
You. you. you.

421
00:30:08.432 --> 00:30:10.309
Well. what are you going to do?

422
00:30:10.434 --> 00:30:12.311
Nothing. just keep training the men.

423
00:30:14.062 --> 00:30:15.564
Am I interrupting?

424
00:30:17.316 --> 00:30:18.900
No. no.

425
00:30:19.443 --> 00:30:21.069
Lieutenant Lewis Nixon.

426
00:30:21.153 --> 00:30:23.697
Lieutenant Harry Welsh. just in from the 82nd.

427
00:30:23.780 --> 00:30:25.073
Congratulations on the promotion.

428
00:30:25.157 --> 00:30:27.075
Thanks. if you want to call it that.

429
00:30:27.701 --> 00:30:29.536
You'll learn him pretty quickly.

430
00:30:29.578 --> 00:30:31.955
No flaws. no vices. no sense of humor.

431
00:30:32.581 --> 00:30:35.459
Just like your chums up at battalion staff.

432
00:30:36.168 --> 00:30:37.336
What's up?

433
00:30:38.170 --> 00:30:39.921
I'm hearing a lot of rumblings.

434
00:30:39.963 --> 00:30:41.089
Sobel?

435
00:30:41.173 --> 00:30:42.716
Just talking about that.

436
00:30:43.342 --> 00:30:46.094
So. he gets a little jumpy in the field?

437
00:30:46.345 --> 00:30:48.555
He gets jumpy and then you get killed.

438
00:30:48.805 --> 00:30:50.182
That's nice.

439
00:30:50.223 --> 00:30:53.602
Yeah. listen. if we discuss it. I think it
should just be amongst ourselves.

440
00:30:53.727 --> 00:30:54.978
Absolutely.

441
00:31:03.236 --> 00:31:04.821
2nd Platoon. ready?

442
00:31:04.863 --> 00:31:05.989
Ready. sir.

443
00:31:07.074 --> 00:31:08.241
Then get them in formation.

444
00:31:08.367 --> 00:31:09.451
We're moving out.

445
00:31:10.577 --> 00:31:11.870
Yes. sir.

446
00:31:36.895 --> 00:31:38.522
Shut up. Cobb.

447
00:31:38.647 --> 00:31:39.898
You got to admit it.

448
00:31:39.981 --> 00:31:41.400
He's got no chance.

449
00:31:41.650 --> 00:31:45.237
Either the Krauts will get him or one of us.

450
00:31:45.612 --> 00:31:47.030
Who. Sobel?

451
00:31:47.489 --> 00:31:49.241
He screwed up one maneuver.

452
00:31:49.533 --> 00:31:52.035
Well. you know. I'm always fumbling with
grenades.

453
00:31:52.160 --> 00:31:55.288
It would be easy if one went off by accident.
you know?

454
00:31:55.372 --> 00:31:58.500
Well. now they must have put him in charge for
a reason.

455
00:31:59.167 --> 00:32:02.504
Yeah. 'cause the Army wouldn't make a mistake.
right?

456
00:32:17.269 --> 00:32:20.063
Going my way? Wherever the train takes me.

457
00:32:20.147 --> 00:32:22.315
Where do you suppose that might be? I haven't
got a clue.

458
00:32:22.399 --> 00:32:23.942
Yeah. come on. take a guess.

459
00:32:24.192 --> 00:32:26.695
Atlantic. Pacific. Atlantic?

460
00:32:27.195 --> 00:32:28.947
I'm not the intelligence officer.

461
00:32:30.449 --> 00:32:34.411
Well. as such. I. of course. know. but if I
told you. I'd have to kill you.

462
00:32:34.578 --> 00:32:35.912
So. don't tell me.

463
00:32:39.332 --> 00:32:40.584
New York City.

464
00:32:40.792 --> 00:32:41.960
Troopship.

465
00:32:42.210 --> 00:32:43.336
England.

466
00:32:46.089 --> 00:32:47.966
We're invading Europe. my friend.

467
00:32:48.967 --> 00:32:50.594
Fortress Europa.

468
00:32:52.721 --> 00:32:54.222
Since when do I drink?

469
00:32:56.433 --> 00:32:59.227
If I thought you'd drink it. I wouldn't offer
it to you.

470
00:33:01.730 --> 00:33:03.106
Nix?

471
00:33:03.607 --> 00:33:06.234
What are you going to do when you get into
combat?

472
00:33:07.986 --> 00:33:10.489
I have every confidence in my scrounging
abilities.

473
00:33:12.115 --> 00:33:16.453
And I have a case of VAT 69 hidden in your
footlocker.

474
00:33:20.499 --> 00:33:21.374
Really?

475
00:33:21.458 --> 00:33:22.209
Oh. yeah.

476
00:33:24.586 --> 00:33:25.754
'Morning.

477
00:33:28.340 --> 00:33:30.258
This could turn into a real nice trip.

478
00:33:46.650 --> 00:33:48.652
"Dear sir or madam:

479
00:33:49.152 --> 00:33:54.115
"Soon your son will drop from the sky to
engage and defeat the enemy.

480
00:33:54.533 --> 00:33:57.410
"Your frequent letters of love and
encouragement...

481
00:33:57.494 --> 00:33:59.913
"...will arm him with a fighting heart.

482
00:34:00.539 --> 00:34:04.501
"With that he cannot fail. but will win glory
for himself...

483
00:34:04.668 --> 00:34:08.171
"...make you proud of him. and his country
ever grateful...

484
00:34:08.255 --> 00:34:10.674
"...for his service in its hour of need.

485
00:34:11.049 --> 00:34:14.427
"Signed. Herbert M. Sobel. Captain
Commanding."

486
00:34:27.482 --> 00:34:31.486
Right now. some lucky bastard's
headed for the South Pacific.

487
00:34:31.570 --> 00:34:32.487
Oh. what I'd give.

488
00:34:32.696 --> 00:34:35.115
He's going to get billeted on some tropical
island.

489
00:34:35.240 --> 00:34:36.116
Keep talking.

490
00:34:36.199 --> 00:34:39.202
Sitting under a palm tree with six naked
native girls...

491
00:34:39.244 --> 00:34:42.956
...helping him cut up coconuts so he can hand-
feed them to the flamingos.

492
00:34:43.623 --> 00:34:45.250
Flamingos are mean.

493
00:34:45.500 --> 00:34:46.585
They bite.

494
00:34:46.626 --> 00:34:48.253
So do the naked native girls.

495
00:34:48.378 --> 00:34:49.504
With any luck.

496
00:34:49.588 --> 00:34:51.840
Hey. guys. I'm glad I'm going to Europe.

497
00:34:52.215 --> 00:34:54.884
Hitler gets one of these right across the
windpipe.

498
00:34:55.010 --> 00:34:58.138
Roosevelt changes Thanksgiving to Joe Toye
Day...

499
00:34:58.221 --> 00:35:01.641
...and pays me $10.000 a year for the rest of
my fucking life.

500
00:35:02.601 --> 00:35:04.394
What if we don't get to Europe?

501
00:35:04.519 --> 00:35:06.354
What if they send us to North Africa?

502
00:35:06.396 --> 00:35:07.522
My brother's in North Africa.

503
00:35:07.606 --> 00:35:08.732
He says it's hot.

504
00:35:08.773 --> 00:35:10.650
Really. it's hot in Africa?

505
00:35:10.734 --> 00:35:12.235
Shut up.

506
00:35:12.277 --> 00:35:14.279
The point is. it don't matter where we go.

507
00:35:14.362 --> 00:35:16.406
In combat. the only person you can trust...

508
00:35:16.489 --> 00:35:18.658
...is yourself and the fellow next to you.

509
00:35:18.742 --> 00:35:21.661
Hey. as long as he's a paratrooper.

510
00:35:21.786 --> 00:35:22.621
Oh. yeah?

511
00:35:22.662 --> 00:35:25.665
And what if that paratrooper turns out to be
Sobel?

512
00:35:25.749 --> 00:35:29.419
If I'm next to Sobel in combat. I'm moving on
down the line.

513
00:35:29.753 --> 00:35:33.548
Hook up with some other officer. like Heyliger
or Winters.

514
00:35:33.632 --> 00:35:35.425
I like Winters. he's a good man.

515
00:35:35.425 --> 00:35:37.427
But when the bullets start flying...

516
00:35:37.510 --> 00:35:40.180
...I don't know if I want a Quaker doing my
fighting for me.

517
00:35:40.263 --> 00:35:42.265
How do you know he's a Quaker?

518
00:35:42.307 --> 00:35:43.516
He ain't Catholic.

519
00:35:43.558 --> 00:35:44.768
Neither is Sobel.

520
00:35:44.809 --> 00:35:46.686
That prick's a son of Abraham.

521
00:35:47.812 --> 00:35:49.064
He's what?

522
00:35:49.314 --> 00:35:50.649
He's a Jew.

523
00:35:54.527 --> 00:35:55.445
I'm a Jew.

524
00:35:56.279 --> 00:35:57.822
Congratulations.

525
00:35:58.198 --> 00:36:00.033
Get your nose out of my face.

526
00:36:07.582 --> 00:36:09.209
What's all that about?

527
00:36:09.459 --> 00:36:11.461
Gonorrhea called Sobel a Jew.

528
00:36:11.711 --> 00:36:14.214
Liebgott took offense 'cause he's a Jew too.

529
00:36:15.715 --> 00:36:18.468
Fighting over Sobel. that's smart.

530
00:36:36.695 --> 00:36:38.113
Attack!

531
00:36:41.491 --> 00:36:43.952
No. you want to kill him!

532
00:36:43.993 --> 00:36:45.954
Parry right. parry left.

533
00:36:46.121 --> 00:36:46.996
Thrust!

534
00:36:47.330 --> 00:36:48.373
Take cover.

535
00:36:48.623 --> 00:36:49.749
Okay.

536
00:36:50.375 --> 00:36:54.129
Yesterday. we talked about magnetic
declination...

537
00:36:54.129 --> 00:36:56.631
...and the "left add. right subtract" rule.

538
00:36:56.631 --> 00:36:58.258
Today we're putting it into practice.

539
00:36:58.633 --> 00:37:01.469
There are two basic types of fighting
positions.

540
00:37:01.761 --> 00:37:04.389
The first is the prepared position.

541
00:37:04.514 --> 00:37:10.228
The advantages of a prepared position are that
it gives you cover and concealment.

542
00:37:10.270 --> 00:37:11.980
Commence fire!

543
00:37:16.276 --> 00:37:19.529
We'll then maneuver right in through these
trees.

544
00:37:19.529 --> 00:37:24.367
At the same time. our second platoon. in this
particular case. moves over here.

545
00:37:24.409 --> 00:37:27.787
He's then going to close with and kill or
capture that German.

546
00:37:52.687 --> 00:37:54.522
Sobel's late.

547
00:38:06.409 --> 00:38:08.077
Why is there a fence here?

548
00:38:10.830 --> 00:38:12.457
There should be no fence here.

549
00:38:13.708 --> 00:38:15.168
Give me the map.

550
00:38:18.213 --> 00:38:19.714
Perconte. Luz.

551
00:38:19.798 --> 00:38:21.716
Get the men. get them...

552
00:38:21.800 --> 00:38:23.468
Take cover behind those trees.

553
00:38:23.593 --> 00:38:25.970
You heard the word. Let's go over there.

554
00:38:29.974 --> 00:38:33.061
There should be no... There should be no fence
here.

555
00:38:33.102 --> 00:38:35.104
We could go over it. sir.

556
00:38:35.605 --> 00:38:36.731
Really?

557
00:38:36.940 --> 00:38:39.192
That's not the point. Where the goddamn...

558
00:38:39.359 --> 00:38:41.319
Where the goddamn hell are we?

559
00:38:43.238 --> 00:38:44.364
Perconte?
Yeah.

560
00:38:44.489 --> 00:38:46.825
Sobel's lost again. right? Yeah. he's lost.

561
00:38:46.866 --> 00:38:47.992
Fucking Christ.

562
00:38:51.996 --> 00:38:53.998
Can you do Major Horton?

563
00:38:54.749 --> 00:38:57.836
Does a wild bear crap in the woods. son?

564
00:38:58.753 --> 00:39:00.880
Maybe the good major can goose this schmuck.

565
00:39:01.005 --> 00:39:02.257
Get us moving?

566
00:39:02.715 --> 00:39:03.716
No way.

567
00:39:03.758 --> 00:39:07.011
Yes. You got to.

568
00:39:07.470 --> 00:39:09.097
All right. just this once.

569
00:39:14.394 --> 00:39:17.647
Three-five-six-eight-three-three.

570
00:39:17.772 --> 00:39:18.898
Isn't that the intersection?

571
00:39:18.982 --> 00:39:20.149
No. sir. it's here.

572
00:39:20.275 --> 00:39:21.609
You're a full grid off.

573
00:39:22.402 --> 00:39:23.862
Goddamn it.

574
00:39:24.028 --> 00:39:26.531
Is there a problem. Captain Sobel?

575
00:39:26.656 --> 00:39:27.740
Who said that?

576
00:39:27.782 --> 00:39:29.158
Who broke silence?

577
00:39:29.617 --> 00:39:31.995
I think it's Major Horton. sir.

578
00:39:34.122 --> 00:39:35.290
Major Horton?

579
00:39:35.415 --> 00:39:37.041
What is he... Did he join us?

580
00:39:37.792 --> 00:39:40.378
I think maybe he's moving between the
platoons. sir.

581
00:39:40.420 --> 00:39:44.299
What is the goddamn holdup. Mr. Sobel?

582
00:39:46.426 --> 00:39:48.386
A fence. sir.

583
00:39:48.803 --> 00:39:49.929
God!

584
00:39:50.305 --> 00:39:52.015
A barbed wire fence.

585
00:39:52.056 --> 00:39:54.142
Oh. that dog just ain't going to hunt!

586
00:39:56.519 --> 00:40:00.690
Now. you cut that fence and get this goddamn
platoon on the move!

587
00:40:02.692 --> 00:40:04.027
Yes. sir!

588
00:40:06.571 --> 00:40:08.656
Where are my goddamn wire cutters?

589
00:40:10.783 --> 00:40:12.035
We have to move.

590
00:40:12.076 --> 00:40:14.579
Sir. without Captain Sobel and 1st Platoon?

591
00:40:15.330 --> 00:40:18.082
It's a T-intersection. We improvise.

592
00:40:18.207 --> 00:40:22.295
Double envelopment laid on a base of fire to
cut the road in all directions.

593
00:40:22.337 --> 00:40:25.924
Hook right with first squad. Tell Guarnere to
move left with second.

594
00:40:25.965 --> 00:40:29.052
I'll be right up the middle with third. go.
Yes. sir.

595
00:40:51.491 --> 00:40:52.951
Deary me.

596
00:41:04.128 --> 00:41:05.588
Bloody hell.

597
00:41:25.233 --> 00:41:27.110
You've done it now. Yanks.

598
00:41:27.652 --> 00:41:29.404
You've captured me.

599
00:41:32.782 --> 00:41:35.493
Hi-ho. Silver!

600
00:41:39.372 --> 00:41:41.290
Would that be the enemy?

601
00:41:41.749 --> 00:41:43.793
As a matter of fact. yes.

602
00:41:52.010 --> 00:41:53.261
Good work. 2nd Platoon.

603
00:41:53.302 --> 00:41:54.679
We took the objective.

604
00:42:03.938 --> 00:42:07.066
Who is the idiot who cut that man's fence?

605
00:42:07.066 --> 00:42:08.276
I was ordered to. sir.

606
00:42:08.317 --> 00:42:09.193
By whom?

607
00:42:09.277 --> 00:42:10.445
Major Horton. sir.

608
00:42:10.528 --> 00:42:11.946
Major Horton? Yes. sir.

609
00:42:12.196 --> 00:42:14.449
Major Horton told you to do that? Yes. sir.

610
00:42:14.782 --> 00:42:17.535
Major Horton ordered you to cut the fence?

611
00:42:18.286 --> 00:42:19.704
Yes. he did.

612
00:42:19.954 --> 00:42:23.458
Major Horton is on leave in London.

613
00:42:26.294 --> 00:42:27.920
Get those cows out of here.

614
00:42:56.991 --> 00:42:58.367
Lieutenant Winters.

615
00:43:01.871 --> 00:43:03.873
With Captain Sobel's compliments. sir.

616
00:43:07.126 --> 00:43:08.252
Lieutenant.

617
00:43:27.605 --> 00:43:29.232
Oh. for crying out loud.

618
00:43:29.524 --> 00:43:31.526
This spells court-martial.

619
00:43:31.526 --> 00:43:33.653
Wide open! Yes.

620
00:43:37.406 --> 00:43:39.408
No. sir. I do not understand.

621
00:43:39.784 --> 00:43:43.246
Your orders to me were to inspect the latrines
at 1000 hours.

622
00:43:43.287 --> 00:43:48.793
From 0930 to 0955 I was censoring the enlisted
men's mail by order of Colonel Strayer.

623
00:43:49.669 --> 00:43:52.797
At 1000 hours I followed your orders to the
minute.

624
00:43:52.880 --> 00:43:55.508
I changed that time to 0945.

625
00:43:55.550 --> 00:43:56.676
No one told me. sir.

626
00:43:56.676 --> 00:43:57.802
I telephoned.

627
00:43:57.885 --> 00:44:00.304
I'm quartered with a family that has no
telephone.

628
00:44:00.388 --> 00:44:01.764
And sent a runner.

629
00:44:01.806 --> 00:44:03.266
No runner found me. Captain.

630
00:44:03.307 --> 00:44:07.562
Irregardless. when given a task
to perform by a ranking officer you

631
00:44:07.562 --> 00:44:11.774
Should have delegated your task
of latrine inspection to another officer.

632
00:44:11.816 --> 00:44:13.276
You failed to do so.

633
00:44:13.568 --> 00:44:17.196
Were I to let such a failure of duty by my own
X O go unpunished...

634
00:44:17.321 --> 00:44:19.574
...what kind of message is that to the men?

635
00:44:19.699 --> 00:44:21.951
I performed my duty as I was ordered. sir.

636
00:44:22.201 --> 00:44:23.661
And I disagree.

637
00:44:23.911 --> 00:44:27.081
So. your options are quite simple. Lieutenant.

638
00:44:27.832 --> 00:44:32.712
Punishment for your offenses will be denial of
a 48-hour pass for 60 days.

639
00:44:32.795 --> 00:44:34.922
Stand before me at attention.

640
00:44:37.967 --> 00:44:42.430
Or you may initiate a letter of appeal and
request a trial by court-martial.

641
00:44:47.310 --> 00:44:49.187
You spend your weekends on the base anyway.
Dick.

642
00:44:49.228 --> 00:44:51.189
Be a man. take the punishment.

643
00:44:52.607 --> 00:44:54.483
May I borrow your pen. sir?

644
00:45:06.495 --> 00:45:07.997
My endorsement. sir.

645
00:45:09.749 --> 00:45:11.751
I request trial by court-martial.

646
00:45:23.387 --> 00:45:25.264
We lost Winters to battalion mess.

647
00:45:25.848 --> 00:45:27.516
You're shitting me. No.

648
00:45:27.642 --> 00:45:31.604
Strayer did it. while they try to figure out
the procedures for his court-martial.

649
00:45:31.646 --> 00:45:33.773
Nix better find a loophole and get him out.

650
00:45:33.856 --> 00:45:34.899
And if he don't?

651
00:45:35.149 --> 00:45:38.861
Winters scrambles eggs while the rest of us
make the big jump with Sobel.

652
00:45:40.655 --> 00:45:41.906
Not me.

653
00:45:42.657 --> 00:45:45.034
So we're going through with this. right?

654
00:45:45.409 --> 00:45:46.994
We've got to do something.

655
00:45:47.036 --> 00:45:48.287
Yeah.

656
00:45:49.914 --> 00:45:50.998
All right.

657
00:45:51.791 --> 00:45:53.042
Good.

658
00:45:54.669 --> 00:45:56.796
But we'd all better be clear on the
consequences.

659
00:45:56.796 --> 00:45:59.048
I don't care about the consequences.

660
00:46:00.424 --> 00:46:03.177
We could be lined up against a wall and shot.

661
00:46:05.179 --> 00:46:07.056
Now. I'm ready to face that.

662
00:46:08.766 --> 00:46:11.018
And every one of us had better be. too.

663
00:46:16.691 --> 00:46:20.152
I will not follow that man into combat.

664
00:46:23.322 --> 00:46:24.448
Me neither.

665
00:46:27.702 --> 00:46:28.703
All right.

666
00:46:30.288 --> 00:46:31.539
Then let's do it.

667
00:46:45.553 --> 00:46:47.054
"I hereby...

668
00:46:48.806 --> 00:46:53.352
"...no longer wish to serve...

669
00:46:56.105 --> 00:46:58.107
"...as a non-commissioned officer...

670
00:47:05.364 --> 00:47:06.866
"...in Easy Company."

671
00:47:20.838 --> 00:47:22.214
All right. boys.

672
00:47:23.215 --> 00:47:24.383
Good luck.

673
00:47:28.846 --> 00:47:30.389
I ought to have you all shot!

674
00:47:31.349 --> 00:47:33.476
This is nothing less than an act of mutiny...

675
00:47:33.517 --> 00:47:36.604
...while we prepare for the goddamn invasion
of Europe.

676
00:47:36.771 --> 00:47:38.272
Sergeant Harris.

677
00:47:38.397 --> 00:47:39.106
Sir.

678
00:47:39.148 --> 00:47:41.150
Turn in your stripes. collect your gear.

679
00:47:41.233 --> 00:47:43.986
You are hereby transferred out of my regiment.

680
00:47:44.236 --> 00:47:44.904
Sir.

681
00:47:44.987 --> 00:47:45.780
Get out.

682
00:47:47.490 --> 00:47:48.783
Sergeant Ranney.

683
00:47:48.908 --> 00:47:50.117
Sir.

684
00:47:50.242 --> 00:47:53.371
You consider yourself lucky. I'm only busting
you to private.

685
00:47:53.537 --> 00:47:57.416
All of you NCOs have disgraced the 101st
Airborne.

686
00:47:57.541 --> 00:48:02.421
Consider yourself lucky that we are on the eve
of the largest action in the history of warfare...

687
00:48:02.546 --> 00:48:06.425
...which leaves me no choice but to spare your
lives.

688
00:48:09.804 --> 00:48:12.556
Now. get out of my office and get out of my
sight.

689
00:48:13.307 --> 00:48:14.308
Get.

690
00:48:31.075 --> 00:48:32.701
Keep them coming. atta-boy.

691
00:49:06.485 --> 00:49:10.114
I can only speculate. sir. Most of the men
would never do this...

692
00:49:10.197 --> 00:49:14.326
...but I believe just a few of the sergeants
may have felt...

693
00:49:14.368 --> 00:49:18.205
...their loyalty lay more to the platoon than
to the company.

694
00:49:19.081 --> 00:49:22.626
And these few sergeants convinced all of the
other NCOs in your company...

695
00:49:22.751 --> 00:49:24.003
...to turn in their stripes?

696
00:49:24.086 --> 00:49:26.005
As staff sergeants. they have a great amount
of influence. sir.

697
00:49:26.130 --> 00:49:27.840
But as I say. the rest are good men.

698
00:49:27.965 --> 00:49:30.342
I know them. I can work with them.

699
00:49:37.475 --> 00:49:39.852
This business with the Winters' court-
martial...

700
00:49:39.894 --> 00:49:42.104
...has been an unpleasant distraction.

701
00:49:42.146 --> 00:49:44.148
Indeed it has. sir.

702
00:49:44.857 --> 00:49:46.358
However...

703
00:49:46.984 --> 00:49:49.778
...your command of Easy Company has been
exemplary.

704
00:49:49.862 --> 00:49:51.655
Thank you. sir.

705
00:49:52.281 --> 00:49:56.660
In fact. except for the actions of a few of
your non-coms...

706
00:49:57.411 --> 00:50:01.916
...I believe you've fielded one of the finest
companies of soldiers I've ever seen.

707
00:50:01.999 --> 00:50:03.167
Yes. sir.

708
00:50:04.502 --> 00:50:07.004
Herbert. Division has established...

709
00:50:07.046 --> 00:50:09.507
...a parachute training school at Chilton
Foliat.

710
00:50:09.548 --> 00:50:13.010
The idea is for non-infantry types who...

711
00:50:13.677 --> 00:50:15.679
...were vital to the coming invasion...

712
00:50:15.763 --> 00:50:19.433
...such as doctors and chaplains. to take jump
training there.

713
00:50:21.060 --> 00:50:23.187
I can't think of anyone more qualified...

714
00:50:23.270 --> 00:50:25.814
...to command such a school than you are.

715
00:50:29.193 --> 00:50:30.694
Sir?

716
00:50:34.031 --> 00:50:36.325
I'm reassigning you to Chilton Foliat.

717
00:50:45.543 --> 00:50:47.461
I'm losing Easy Company?

718
00:50:47.586 --> 00:50:49.588
The war effort needs you elsewhere.

719
00:50:56.679 --> 00:50:58.180
Permission to speak. sir?

720
00:50:58.347 --> 00:50:59.473
Granted.

721
00:51:03.936 --> 00:51:06.480
Is... Who will be replacing me?

722
00:51:06.689 --> 00:51:09.858
Lieutenant Meehan from Baker Company is
senior.

723
00:51:12.444 --> 00:51:14.363
Good luck at Chilton Foliat. Herbert.

724
00:51:14.613 --> 00:51:16.073
Don't let us down now.

725
00:51:22.997 --> 00:51:23.998
No. sir.

726
00:51:31.380 --> 00:51:33.132
Carry on.

727
00:52:26.435 --> 00:52:27.895
2nd Platoon. listen up.

728
00:52:27.936 --> 00:52:30.773
I want the first squad and A-side tents right
up there.

729
00:52:31.315 --> 00:52:33.692
Third squad. second row...

730
00:52:48.207 --> 00:52:49.958
Holy shit.

731
00:52:51.335 --> 00:52:53.212
No. it's all right. We're tommies...

732
00:52:53.337 --> 00:52:54.713
...not bleeding boche.

733
00:52:54.797 --> 00:52:55.964
Is all this real?

734
00:52:56.090 --> 00:52:57.049
Yeah. yeah.

735
00:52:57.091 --> 00:52:59.843
Some is from the Hermans. somebody's tailor's
knocked up.

736
00:52:59.927 --> 00:53:02.846
For you. so you can get your mince pies on
this Jerry clobber...

737
00:53:02.930 --> 00:53:04.223
...if you know what I mean.

738
00:53:04.431 --> 00:53:05.474
Not really.

739
00:53:05.933 --> 00:53:07.351
Mack. you got a Luger?

740
00:53:07.476 --> 00:53:09.103
I'm dying to get a real Luger.

741
00:53:09.228 --> 00:53:10.437
Yeah. go on then.

742
00:53:12.606 --> 00:53:14.108
A quick butchers. yeah?

743
00:53:18.112 --> 00:53:20.072
Boy. she sure is a doozy.

744
00:53:20.114 --> 00:53:21.448
Yeah. it's pukka. ain't it?

745
00:53:21.490 --> 00:53:22.366
What?

746
00:53:23.867 --> 00:53:25.452
Hey. Petty.

747
00:53:25.828 --> 00:53:27.246
Hey. mate.

748
00:53:28.997 --> 00:53:31.834
You're having a bath if you think you're half-
inching that.

749
00:53:32.584 --> 00:53:33.627
Oh. yeah.

750
00:53:33.711 --> 00:53:35.379
Sorry. Well. good luck.

751
00:53:35.629 --> 00:53:36.714
You too. mate.

752
00:53:38.382 --> 00:53:39.842
What's up. Hoobs?

753
00:53:40.759 --> 00:53:44.763
These men have been through the toughest
training the Army has to offer.

754
00:53:44.888 --> 00:53:46.974
Under the worst possible circumstances.

755
00:53:48.100 --> 00:53:49.601
And they volunteered for it.

756
00:53:49.643 --> 00:53:52.771
Christ. I was just shooting craps with them.
It's not like...

757
00:53:52.855 --> 00:53:54.648
You know why they volunteered?

758
00:53:54.732 --> 00:53:59.653
So. when things got really bad. the man next
to them would be the best.

759
00:54:00.279 --> 00:54:02.781
Not some draftee who's going to get him
killed.

760
00:54:02.906 --> 00:54:04.867
Are you ticked because they like me?

761
00:54:05.284 --> 00:54:07.911
Because I'm spending time to get to know my
soldiers?

762
00:54:07.995 --> 00:54:10.914
You've been with these guys for what. two
years?

763
00:54:10.998 --> 00:54:12.541
I've been here for six days.

764
00:54:13.917 --> 00:54:15.043
You're gambling. Bob.

765
00:54:15.127 --> 00:54:16.920
So what? Soldiers do that.

766
00:54:17.045 --> 00:54:18.922
I don't deserve a reprimand for it.

767
00:54:19.423 --> 00:54:21.008
What if you'd won?

768
00:54:22.676 --> 00:54:25.804
What? What if you'd won?

769
00:54:30.934 --> 00:54:34.563
Never put yourself in a position where you can
take from these men.

770
00:54:40.068 --> 00:54:41.153
Lieutenant Meehan?

771
00:54:41.195 --> 00:54:42.196
Enter.

772
00:54:44.823 --> 00:54:48.076
On the last training jump. I had a compass.

773
00:54:49.453 --> 00:54:51.079
Close the flap.

774
00:54:53.332 --> 00:54:54.291
Then we turn left.

775
00:54:54.333 --> 00:54:55.334
Yeah.

776
00:54:55.417 --> 00:54:58.170
Bearing zero-four-two.

777
00:54:58.337 --> 00:54:59.463
12 minutes.

778
00:54:59.546 --> 00:55:01.048
Then another left?

779
00:55:02.341 --> 00:55:04.718
Call it three-five-eight...

780
00:55:05.969 --> 00:55:07.596
...for 10 and a half minutes.

781
00:55:08.430 --> 00:55:10.974
Green light. right over Ramsbury.

782
00:55:11.058 --> 00:55:12.100
Ramsbury.

783
00:55:12.226 --> 00:55:13.852
Every single time.

784
00:55:14.728 --> 00:55:18.190
Linear distance on the grid of about...

785
00:55:20.984 --> 00:55:21.860
Okay.

786
00:55:21.860 --> 00:55:22.945
Ramsbury.

787
00:55:24.488 --> 00:55:25.697
Upottery.

788
00:55:33.372 --> 00:55:34.373
So
...

789
00:55:35.707 --> 00:55:36.875
It's Normandy.

790
00:55:38.126 --> 00:55:39.336
St. Marie du Mont.

791
00:55:39.378 --> 00:55:40.963
Causeway Number One.

792
00:55:41.088 --> 00:55:42.714
Causeway Number Two.

793
00:55:42.756 --> 00:55:44.466
The ultimate field problem.

794
00:55:45.717 --> 00:55:48.887
The estuary of the Douve River divides two
beachheads...

795
00:55:48.887 --> 00:55:52.516
...code-named Utah. here. and Omaha. here.

796
00:55:53.225 --> 00:55:55.894
Seaborne Infantry will hit these beaches in
force...

797
00:55:55.978 --> 00:55:58.146
...at a date and time to be specified.

798
00:55:58.605 --> 00:56:00.732
H-hour. D-day.

799
00:56:00.899 --> 00:56:05.153
Airborne's objective. gentlemen. is to take
the town of Carentan...

800
00:56:05.237 --> 00:56:09.116
...thus linking Utah and Omaha into a single.
continuous beachhead.

801
00:56:09.157 --> 00:56:12.619
...linking Omaha and Utah into one continuous
beachhead.

802
00:56:13.287 --> 00:56:16.164
Each trooper will learn this operation by
heart...

803
00:56:16.248 --> 00:56:19.668
...and know his and every other outfits'
mission to the detail.

804
00:56:19.793 --> 00:56:20.544
Meehan?

805
00:56:20.627 --> 00:56:21.795
Yes. Dukeman.

806
00:56:21.879 --> 00:56:23.171
Sir. are we dropping tonight?

807
00:56:23.255 --> 00:56:25.257
When it's time for you to know. we'll let you
know.

808
00:56:25.299 --> 00:56:29.887
In the meantime. study these sand tables.
maps. and reconnaissance photos...

809
00:56:29.928 --> 00:56:32.681
...until you can draw a map of the area by
memory.

810
00:56:32.931 --> 00:56:39.646
Now. we will drop behind this Atlantic wall
five hours before the 4th Infantry lands at Utah.

811
00:56:39.688 --> 00:56:42.941
And between our assembly area and the
battalion's objective...

812
00:56:43.066 --> 00:56:47.321
...there is a German garrison right here in
this area. St. Marie du Mont.

813
00:56:47.654 --> 00:56:50.949
Easy Company will destroy that garrison.

814
00:56:53.410 --> 00:56:57.039
Three-day supply of K rations. chocolate bars.
charms. candy...

815
00:56:57.080 --> 00:56:59.082
...powdered coffee. sugar. and matches.

816
00:56:59.166 --> 00:57:03.086
Compass. bayonet. entrenching tool.
ammunition. gas mask.

817
00:57:03.211 --> 00:57:07.591
Musette bag with ammo. my webbing. my.45.
canteen...

818
00:57:07.674 --> 00:57:09.092
...two cartons of smokes.

819
00:57:09.176 --> 00:57:12.179
Hawkins mine. two grenades.
smoke grenade. gamma grenade...

820
00:57:12.220 --> 00:57:15.849
...TNT. this bullshit. and a pair of nasty
skivvies.

821
00:57:15.933 --> 00:57:16.975
What's your point?

822
00:57:17.100 --> 00:57:18.477
This weighs as much as I do.

823
00:57:18.477 --> 00:57:21.605
I've still got my chute. my reserve chute. my
Mae West. my M-1.

824
00:57:21.605 --> 00:57:23.857
Where are you keeping your brass knuckles?

825
00:57:24.358 --> 00:57:26.318
I could use some brass knuckles.

826
00:57:27.110 --> 00:57:28.487
Hey. anything for me?

827
00:57:28.487 --> 00:57:31.823
Sergeant Martin.

828
00:57:38.580 --> 00:57:40.332
For Talbert.

829
00:57:44.586 --> 00:57:45.629
Heavy! condoms?

830
00:57:45.712 --> 00:57:47.089
I don't know. probably.

831
00:57:47.130 --> 00:57:48.006
What you got?

832
00:57:48.090 --> 00:57:50.634
"Dear Floyd: Give them hell."

833
00:57:51.134 --> 00:57:52.886
It's from the chief of the Kokomo Police.

834
00:57:53.011 --> 00:57:54.012
Right.

835
00:57:57.891 --> 00:57:59.726
You've got to love cops.

836
00:57:59.893 --> 00:58:01.979
All right. listen up. listen up.

837
00:58:02.646 --> 00:58:06.733
If you did not sign your GI life insurance
policy...

838
00:58:07.025 --> 00:58:11.488
...you go on over and see Sergeant Evans at
the headquarters company tent.

839
00:58:12.656 --> 00:58:16.118
You boys don't let your families miss out on
$10.000.

840
00:58:17.160 --> 00:58:18.286
You hear that. Gerry?

841
00:58:18.370 --> 00:58:19.162
Hey. Lip?

842
00:58:19.246 --> 00:58:20.163
Yeah. boy.

843
00:58:23.166 --> 00:58:25.293
Has Guarnere said anything about his brother?

844
00:58:25.377 --> 00:58:26.294
No.

845
00:58:26.378 --> 00:58:27.546
I got a problem.

846
00:58:28.130 --> 00:58:31.550
My wife keeps up with things back home.
casualty lists and like that.

847
00:58:31.633 --> 00:58:32.676
Yeah?

848
00:58:32.926 --> 00:58:34.553
Guarnere's brother in Italy?

849
00:58:34.636 --> 00:58:35.804
Henry?

850
00:58:36.054 --> 00:58:37.556
Killed in Monte Cassino.

851
00:58:39.558 --> 00:58:41.143
Well. I'm sure he doesn't know.

852
00:58:41.184 --> 00:58:42.060
Damn.

853
00:58:42.060 --> 00:58:43.770
What'd you think I should do?

854
00:58:45.063 --> 00:58:47.315
If it were me. I'd tell him.

855
00:58:47.941 --> 00:58:49.943
Couple of hours before we jump?

856
00:58:51.153 --> 00:58:52.904
I don't know.

857
00:59:02.080 --> 00:59:04.583
Why are they springing these things on us now?

858
00:59:05.333 --> 00:59:08.336
It's just an extra 80 pounds strapped to your
leg.

859
00:59:08.670 --> 00:59:12.049
Does anybody have any idea how the hell this
thing works?

860
00:59:12.841 --> 00:59:14.926
Colonel Sink.

861
00:59:16.803 --> 00:59:18.096
Colonel Sink.

862
00:59:20.599 --> 00:59:22.559
"Soldiers of the regiment.

863
00:59:22.934 --> 00:59:27.981
"Tonight is the night of nights.

864
00:59:28.857 --> 00:59:31.068
"Today. as you read this...

865
00:59:31.234 --> 00:59:34.988
"...you are en route to the great adventure
for which you have trained...

866
00:59:35.072 --> 00:59:37.115
"...for over two years."

867
00:59:37.365 --> 00:59:39.367
So. that's why they gave us ice cream.

868
00:59:42.245 --> 00:59:44.623
Easy Company. listen up!

869
00:59:47.125 --> 00:59:49.878
Channel coast is socked in with rain and fog.

870
00:59:50.337 --> 00:59:52.506
No jump tonight.

871
00:59:53.215 --> 00:59:55.258
The invasion has been postponed.

872
00:59:55.634 --> 00:59:57.761
We're on a 24-hour stand-down.

873
01:00:02.015 --> 01:00:03.767
Well. this is quite a surprise.

874
01:00:03.850 --> 01:00:05.018
Not particularly.

875
01:00:05.143 --> 01:00:07.145
It so happens I rather expected it.

876
01:00:07.646 --> 01:00:13.485
Well. I can't see how you people can pass up
$80.000 for the Cause.

877
01:00:13.527 --> 01:00:14.653
For whose cause?

878
01:00:15.487 --> 01:00:17.614
If you're so interested in serving a cause...

879
01:00:17.656 --> 01:00:18.990
...why don't you join the Army?

880
01:00:19.032 --> 01:00:20.534
Next. please.

881
01:00:24.746 --> 01:00:25.664
Oh. 4F.

882
01:00:25.789 --> 01:00:27.165
You look 1A to me.

883
01:00:27.249 --> 01:00:29.167
You don't look so bad yourself.

884
01:00:30.669 --> 01:00:32.170
"Dearest Johnny"?

885
01:00:33.296 --> 01:00:35.048
Well. should you be giving blood?

886
01:00:35.173 --> 01:00:36.299
I woke up.

887
01:00:38.176 --> 01:00:40.303
I got the wrong goddamn jacket.

888
01:00:41.179 --> 01:00:43.014
I was struck by lightning.

889
01:00:50.772 --> 01:00:51.940
Nobody dancing.

890
01:00:52.649 --> 01:00:54.151
It doesn't matter.

891
01:00:54.943 --> 01:00:57.529
"Your pal. Bill Guarnere's brother..."

892
01:02:30.538 --> 01:02:31.790
Good luck. lads.

893
01:02:32.123 --> 01:02:33.250
See you. tommies.

894
01:02:33.792 --> 01:02:35.543
See you. mate.

895
01:02:48.306 --> 01:02:50.517
Try and get these leg straps through.

896
01:02:55.272 --> 01:02:56.773
Johnny?

897
01:03:02.821 --> 01:03:05.031
Got something you might be looking for.

898
01:03:05.573 --> 01:03:07.409
Took your jacket by mistake.

899
01:03:07.450 --> 01:03:08.660
I'm sorry.

900
01:03:08.702 --> 01:03:10.161
You read it?

901
01:03:12.289 --> 01:03:14.082
Where the fuck is Monte Cassino?

902
01:03:14.332 --> 01:03:16.084
I don't know. Italy somewhere.

903
01:03:19.963 --> 01:03:22.299
Sorry about your brother. Bill.

904
01:03:22.841 --> 01:03:24.592
I'm sorry for my ma.

905
01:03:25.468 --> 01:03:27.220
He was...

906
01:03:31.599 --> 01:03:33.184
Let's get this over with.

907
01:03:37.230 --> 01:03:38.690
Bill?

908
01:03:41.443 --> 01:03:43.361
I'll meet up with you over there.

909
01:03:47.699 --> 01:03:50.618
Gentlemen. Doc Roe is handing these out for
air sickness.

910
01:03:50.702 --> 01:03:54.581
Orders are. "Every man takes one now. another.
30 minutes in the air."

911
01:03:56.374 --> 01:03:57.500
Lieutenant.

912
01:04:04.382 --> 01:04:05.759
2nd Platoon. listen up.

913
01:04:09.637 --> 01:04:10.764
Good luck.

914
01:04:12.390 --> 01:04:13.975
God bless you.

915
01:04:15.727 --> 01:04:17.645
I'll see you in the assembly area.

916
01:05:12.659 --> 01:05:16.830
If the wire contacts are sensitive. then I
think all we should have to do...

917
01:05:22.710 --> 01:05:23.711
Goddamn. Lieb.

918
01:05:23.837 --> 01:05:25.797
That airsick pill is making me loopy.

918
01:05:26.305 --> 01:06:26.340
